feature/decodeC-ssum-defer 2026-09-19T15:35:00Z
agent: claude-code
heartbeat: 2026-09-19T15:35:00Z
status: in-progress
done-so-far: found while investigating stackbytes-json-read-not-flat-
  on-aarch64 — Json.decodeC and Cbor.getC's SSum case call the
  recursive decode directly (decodeC(sc(), v).map(...) /
  getC(in, sc()).map(...)) instead of wrapping it in Cont.defer, the
  only recursive case in either fold that doesn't. Empirically this
  costs one extra native frame per Sum dispatch, not unbounded growth
  (Schema.derived always wraps a case's payload in a product, whose
  own field IS deferred one level in) — verified with a probe:
  recursive Expr enum (Lit | Neg(Expr)) at depth 500 on 256 KB stack,
  GREEN on this machine. Does not explain the original container
  discrepancy (Tree has no sum type); worth fixing anyway for
  consistency and defensiveness (a hand-written Schema instance where
  a case's payload recurses directly, not through a product, would
  hit it)
next: add Cont.defer around both call sites, add the probe as a
  permanent regression test, verify, gate, land
